{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbgfExk8R25gEcXPJDHm", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "`git rebase --onto` lets you choose the **new base** for a set of commits separately from **which commits get moved**. A plain `git rebase <upstream>` can't do that.\n\n### Syntax\n\n```\ngit rebase --onto <newbase> <upstream> [<branch>]\n```\n\nGit takes the commits that are in `<branch>` (default: the current branch) but **not** in `<upstream>`, which is the range `upstream..branch`. It replays them on top of `<newbase>`, then moves `<branch>` to point at the result.\n\nA plain `git rebase main` is shorthand for `git rebase --onto main main`.\n\n### Example: move a branch off another feature branch\n\nYou branched `feature-b` from `feature-a`, but `feature-b` doesn't actually depend on it:\n\n```\nmain:       A---B\n                 \\\nfeature-a:        C---D\n                       \\\nfeature-b:              E---F\n```\n\nYou want only `E` and `F` to sit on `main`:\n\n```\ngit rebase --onto main feature-a feature-b\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```\nmain:       A---B\n                |\\\nfeature-a:      | C---D\n                 \\\nfeature-b:        E'---F'\n```\n\n`E'` and `F'` are new commits with the same changes but new hashes. `C` and `D` stay on `feature-a` and don't come along.\n\n### Other common uses\n\n- **Drop commits from the middle of a branch:** `git rebase --onto HEAD~3 HEAD~1` removes the two commits `HEAD~2` and `HEAD~1` but keeps `HEAD`.\n- **Recover after an upstream branch was rebased or squashed:** `git rebase --onto main <old-feature-a-tip>` replays only your own commits onto the rewritten base.\n\n### Caveats\n\n- It rewrites history, so be careful with branches other people have already pulled. If you need to push afterwards, use `git push --force-with-lease`.\n- If something goes wrong, you can undo it with `git rebase --abort` while the rebase is still running, or with `git reset --hard ORIG_HEAD` right after it finishes."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7215, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16780, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7215}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ace00b59-e905-4462-a9ec-f5da632b7359", "uuid": "9386d478-d634-44d1-b51a-741ac2ca1387", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T14:35:49.059Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbgfEdPkR6m9PNCu7qeq"}
